## 3. Things You Don't Know Are Broken

### 🐛 Real Bugs

| Issue | File | Details |
|---|---|---|
| **Token leaked in URL** | [student page.tsx:76](file:///c:/Users/chatz/Downloads/AST/ast4-lesson-builder/app/dashboard/student/page.tsx#L76), [programs page.tsx:105](file:///c:/Users/chatz/Downloads/AST/ast4-lesson-builder/app/dashboard/student/programs/page.tsx#L105) | `router.push(/viewer/${lessonId}?userId=${user_id}&token=${token})` — The JWT token is passed as a **URL query parameter**. This is a security vulnerability: tokens in URLs get logged in server access logs, browser history, analytics, and proxy logs. Move to an auth header or cookie. |
| **Progress page redefines [cn()](file:///c:/Users/chatz/Downloads/AST/ast4-lesson-builder/app/dashboard/student/progress/page.tsx#175-178)** | [progress page.tsx:175-177](file:///c:/Users/chatz/Downloads/AST/ast4-lesson-builder/app/dashboard/student/progress/page.tsx#L175-L177) | Defines its own [cn()](file:///c:/Users/chatz/Downloads/AST/ast4-lesson-builder/app/dashboard/student/progress/page.tsx#175-178) function at the bottom instead of importing from `@/lib/utils`. This version just joins strings and doesn't handle Tailwind class conflicts (no `clsx` + `twMerge`). |
| **Sidebar collapse doesn't update main content padding** | [student layout.tsx:29](file:///c:/Users/chatz/Downloads/AST/ast4-lesson-builder/app/dashboard/student/layout.tsx#L29) | Layout hardcodes `md:pl-[80px] lg:pl-[280px]` but the sidebar collapse state isn't shared. When sidebar is expanded on [md](file:///c:/Users/chatz/Downloads/AST/ast4-lesson-builder/README.md) screens, content is hidden underneath because it only has 80px padding. |
| **Avatar "Update Seed" hover** | [settings page.tsx:53-55](file:///c:/Users/chatz/Downloads/AST/ast4-lesson-builder/app/dashboard/student/settings/page.tsx#L53-L55) | Shows "Update Seed" text on hover but has no click handler. Users expect to upload a profile photo, not "update a seed." |
| **`AnimatePresence` without `key` on conditionals** | [student page.tsx:164](file:///c:/Users/chatz/Downloads/AST/ast4-lesson-builder/app/dashboard/student/page.tsx#L164) | `AnimatePresence mode="popLayout"` wraps mapped items but the empty-state div doesn't have a motion wrapper, so exit animations won't work properly. |
| **Dashboard header duplicated** | Layout includes `<DashboardHeader />` but some pages also import it (unused import in programs page). Potential for double-render if not careful. |

### ⚠️ Architecture & UX Gaps

| Issue | Impact |
|---|---|
| **No loading skeleton / shimmer states** | Every page shows a spinner + military text ("Syncing Directives..."). Use skeleton cards for perceived performance. |
| **No error boundaries** | If any API call fails, console.error is the only handling. No user-facing error states except on the student overview. |
| **No empty state illustrations** | Empty lists show a text-only message. Use friendly illustrations or SVGs. |
| **No breadcrumb on most pages** | Only the Programs page has breadcrumbs. Students lose context on other pages. |
| **No "last accessed" or "continue where you left off"** | The "Resume Session" button just opens the first lesson in the array, not the most recent one. |
| **No offline/network-down handling** | If the backend is unreachable, pages spin forever. |
| **No pagination** | Student overview shows `lessons.slice(0, 6)` hardcoded. If a student has 50+ lessons, they can't see them. |
| **Tutor cannot see individual student progress** | The "Students" link in tutor sidebar goes to `/dashboard/tutor/students` but there's no student detail view for tutors to understand how individual students are doing. |
| **No confirmation/toast on actions** | Register, unregister, save — no success/error feedback toast. Users don't know if their action worked. |
| **Program cards don't show instructor/author info** | Students have no idea who created or teaches the program. |
| **No responsive testing on the catalog details view** | The `lg:grid-cols-3` layout breaks on tablet — the sticky sidebar overlaps content. |

